{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nIn the rebar-mcp container the compaction trigger's sidecars, the worker lock `compact-worker.lock` and the last-sweep stamp `compact-sweep.stamp`, live in `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar/` (`StorePaths(tracker).sidecar`, via `_trigger_lock_path`/`_sweep_stamp_path` in src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py). That directory is the sibling of the tracker `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`, and it is not mounted: the container mounts only `gerrit_mcp_tickets`, `gerrit_mcp_code`, `/var/lib/rebar` and two secrets. Confirmed read-only over SSM on 2026-11-04 against rebar-mcp-fe6c2100292c-8093: `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar` does not exist 11 minutes after start, while `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets/.git` (on the `gerrit_mcp_tickets` volume) already holds `rebar-compact-intents/`, `rebar-fetch.lock` and `rebar-git-op.lock`.\n\nConsequences, by the code's own rules:\n- Each blue-green deploy starts with no stamp, and `_sweep_is_stale` treats a missing stamp as stale, so the first close after every deploy fires a full sweep regardless of `compact.trigger_interval_s` (6 h).\n- During the blue-green overlap the old and new containers each have their own `compact-worker.lock` over the one shared `gerrit_mcp_tickets` clone, so the \"one worker at a time\" lock does not span them.\n\n## Measured frequency\nFrom the MCP clone's own reflog (read-only, 2026-08-27 to 2026-11-03: 633 `ticket: COMPACT` commits in 90 bursts; 233 MCP deploys from the autodeploy journal in that range): 49 deploys were followed by a folding sweep before the next deploy, and in 26 of those the first sweep started less than 6 h after the previous one. That is an upper bound for stamp-loss sweeps: the per-ticket arm also fires sweeps, and a sweep that folds nothing leaves no commit. No deploy had a sweep in flight at cutover with a second sweep starting inside the 21-minute retire window, so overlapping sweeps are not observed in this evidence. The sweep logs nothing on success, so the journal since Gerrit 3300 has no sweep lines to count.\n\n## Approach\nFollow `intangible-ladyish-vicuna`'s precedent: key the sidecars on the STORE, never on whatever sits beside it. Move the trigger lock and the sweep stamp into the tracker's git dir (`StorePaths(tracker).git_dir`), as `rebar-compact-worker.lock` and `rebar-compact-sweep.stamp`, beside the compaction intent journal and the fetch/git-op locks already there. That directory is part of the store itself, so it persists on the store's volume, is shared by every process using the store (both MCP containers, every local worktree view), stays out of commits and `git status`, and needs no compose or autodeploy change. `src/rebar/_store/push_state.py` already keeps its marker there for the same reason.\n\n- `compact_trigger._trigger_lock_path` / `_sweep_stamp_path` derive from `StorePaths.git_dir`; `record_sweep` and `_acquire_trigger_lock` stop creating `.rebar/` for them. The worker log stays in `.rebar/logs` (the MCP container already routes it to the journal).\n- `doctor_locks` reports the compaction leg from the same helper, so `rebar doctor` and the sweep never disagree about the path.\n- Cross-container behaviour: the stamped lock already refuses a holder in another PID namespace (reclaim only after the existing 1 h age ceiling), and Gerrit 3276's `stop_local_sweep` already leaves an \"other pid namespace\" stamp alone. Its commit message assumed exactly this shared stamp, so retirement still signals only the server's own worker.\n- One-time upgrade effect: the old `.rebar` stamp is not read, so each store gets one extra sweep after upgrade; a sweep still running from the old version holds the old path once. The store write lock keeps both safe.\n\n## Scope\nIn: src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py, src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py, their tests (tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py, tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py, tests/unit/test_mcp_retire_sweep.py if path fixtures move), docs that name the sidecar path.\nOut: the other `.rebar` sidecars (HLC state, recent-creates journal, snapshot-GC lock); filed separately if they show the same per-container effect.\n\n## Testing\n- A regression test where 2 trigger processes, started through `tests/_subprocess_env.subprocess_env` and each bounded, share one store but have different `.rebar` sidecar dirs (a symlinked tracker view per process): before the fix both acquire the lock; after, the second is refused, and a stamp written by one is read as fresh by the other.\n- Unit tests that the lock and stamp paths live in the tracker's git dir for a plain clone and for a linked-worktree `.git` file.\n- `retire_local_sweep`/`stop_local_sweep` tests still pass against the moved stamp, including the foreign-namespace refusal.\n- Targeted modules: compaction trigger, stamped lock, doctor locks, MCP retire/shutdown; then `make lint` and `make typecheck` with the worktree `.venv/bin` first on PATH.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The trigger lock and sweep stamp live in the tracker's git dir, so they survive a blue-green deploy and are shared by both MCP containers during the overlap; two processes with different `.rebar` dirs over one store exclude each other (regression test).\n- [ ] A sweep stamp written through one view of the store reads as fresh through another, so a fresh container or worktree does not re-fire a sweep the store just had.\n- [ ] `stop_local_sweep` still signals only a worker in its own PID namespace and leaves another container's stamp alone (existing tests green against the new path).\n- [ ] `rebar doctor`'s compaction-worker row reports the new lock path.\n- [ ] Targeted tests, `make lint` and `make typecheck` are green; every `src/rebar` file stays at 800 lines or fewer.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] After deploy, the live MCP container's tickets git dir holds the compaction stamp after a sweep, and `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar` is not used for it."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793796372104923001,"uuid":"44aa2c5c-f29c-49fe-b3a5-d4e153672e0d"}